id: pm-rl-ip21
title: "Live acceptance: two tev1:4b generations through npm run test:live"
description: "Add npm run test:live (excluded from CI and from the coverage gate) that runs two real training generations of the System One decision-model loop against the locally served frozen model, showing changed checkpoints and the promoted successor collecting, and paste the measured numbers (accuracy and ECE before vs after, endpoint latency, token usage) into a pm comment on the adapter feature."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: execution,live-acceptance,llm-adapter,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:32:39.873Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T13:16:10.933Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: pi-glm
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "npm run test:live executes two real generations against the configured endpoint and model, asserts the candidate checkpoint changes each generation and that generation two collects with generation one's promoted checkpoint, and prints measured before/after accuracy, ECE, latency and token totals; npm test and the coverage gate never invoke the live suite; the measured numbers are recorded as a pm comment on the adapter feature item"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:21:48.391Z",codex-sol,"Live acceptance first run PASS: two real tev1:4b generations promoted; generation 2 collection component equals generation 1 candidate checkpoint. Held-out accuracy 1.0 -> 1.0 in both generations; ECE 0.3329814443 -> 0.2927389850 -> 0.2411651910. Sampled held-out means 0.66375 -> 0.70685 and 0.709475 -> 0.761025. Changed checkpoints 77bb31851756 then a66accd456bf. Eight endpoint requests, 1094 reported tokens, wall elapsed 23189.12 ms (2898.64 ms per query including tracker/training overhead). Endpoint-only latency instrumentation is being added and will be rerun. This two-item synthetic held-out split measures adaptive validation, not an independent benchmark."
  "2026-10-05T06:05:09.301Z",codex-sol,"Final live receipt: npm run test:live passed twice against tev1:4b; both generations promoted and successor collection used the first promoted checkpoint. Accuracy 1.0 to 1.0 in both generations; ECE 0.33298144430342114 to 0.292738985014186 to 0.24116519096373423. Held-out sampled means 0.66375 to 0.70685 and 0.709475 to 0.761025. Tokens 547 per generation, 1094 total across eight queries. Repeat wall time 26157.710259 ms; endpoint time 23302.171132 ms, 2912.7713915 ms per query. Distinct digests and original numbers are in prior comments. Final release gate passed 387 tests and four 100% coverage metrics across 23 source files; PM-linked deterministic acceptance passed. Added packaged System One configuration and measured validation document."
  "2026-10-05T06:09:57.803Z",codex-sol,"Live acceptance evidence and packaged System One example are published in draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/62. Repeat final tarball acceptance passes in npm/Node and Bun. The 23 authored source files are unchanged from the full 387-test four-metric release gate. Claim released; feature remains open for verification."
  "2026-10-13T12:06:24.823Z",codex-agent,"Implement a fresh two-generation live receipt with retained per-query PM evidence, explicit promotion decisions and checkpoint lineage. Keep unit/integration tests on synthetic HTTP servers, live execution opt-in and bounded to 15 minutes. Check adversarial contamination, checkpoint and endpoint failure paths; run npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-13T12:26:07.320Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: remove only the new num_gpu CPU preflight condition while retaining signatures and tests. npm run build succeeds; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"CPU validation\" test/live-systemone.test.ts fails with Missing expected rejection. Restore the guard for final gates. Live cold-load attempts have failed closed before training; retain their partial trackers and retry only within the bounded local CPU execution window."
  "2026-10-13T12:51:46.197Z",codex-agent,Move the watchdog into a minimal launcher so its hard process deadline also includes SDK imports and startup. The worker has the shared AbortSignal; the parent terminates it at 895000 ms and escalates within the remaining five seconds. Permit a declared CPU allocation of one to four threads with num_gpu 0 and per-response zero-VRAM checks. Earlier cold-load and two-thread scoring attempts failed before any promotion; final live and exact-source gates remain pending.
  "2026-10-13T13:11:48.302Z",codex-agent,"Fresh npm run test:live PASS with an isolated loopback CPU service over the existing tev1:4b Q8_0 weights. Two promotions, eight queries, 1094 tokens, 838542.232476 ms worker time under the 900000 ms whole-command watchdog. Seed f40ae63747108d680e70fa6b092b50473fdea6ee3a65e81d717ce48d60881e25 -> generation one 0a0eeb54d990640fbdefad6f501b30df7ff94fe0a634f9a464247770568b2718 -> generation two 9d499e5b1276d95e687bfafebdedca7a2820dafcd9cf94400727c2ca97621037. Both canonical checkpoint files hash to these policy identities. Generation two records the first candidate as its collecting policy. Detailed notes contain dataset and collection digests, all eight decision receipts, calibrated held-out measurements and true promotion decisions. Final npm and Bun release gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-13T13:16:10.933Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked offline acceptance now PASS: pm test pm-rl-ip21 --run --progress executed all three tests without failures or skips, including real HTTP two-generation lineage/checkpoint receipts, persisted invalid-checkpoint refusal, CPU preflight/runner rejection, and the import-time watchdog. The source-scoped npm gate is running; a prior shorter linked-test deadline expired under shared host load. Linked test timeout is now 1800 seconds for the offline suite only; npm run test:live remains hard bounded to 900000 ms."
